            <div xml:id="d409-a2">

                <pb facs="0554" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg452"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have just learned that Mr.
                    Martin J. Iorns, an American horticulturist, arrived yesterday in our harbor on
                    the French steamer, and wishing to come ashore, he was prevented by the
                    commandant of the port.</p>
                <p>I regret very much that that officer should commit such a breach against the
                    orders that he had received and of which I had previously informed you.</p>
                <p>In hastening to assure you that that officer will be punished as he deserves, I
                    take this occasion to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Borno.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
